---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { allQuestions, allPapers } from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="About this site" context="about" description="Who runs physicsaleveltutor.com and where the questions, mark schemes and ratings come from.">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p>physicsaleveltutor.com is run by {site.company}, an A-level tutoring business with a small team of specialist tutors. The site exists to give AQA physics students the past-paper material they actually use, sorted the way they revise, free and without sign-up; and to introduce students who want more help to a tutor who teaches the AQA specification every week.</p>
  <h2>Where the material comes from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Questions, mark schemes and examiner comments</strong> are from AQA's own published papers for every Physics series since June 2016 (7407 AS from 2016, 7408 A level from 2017): {allPapers.length} papers and {allQuestions.length.toLocaleString()} question parts. Each part has been tagged to the specification statements it assesses, its maths and practical skills, any required practical, and its question type. Where a part needs a figure, table or graph printed in an earlier part of the question, that earlier part folds out above it.</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty ratings</strong> (Easy and Hard) come from AQA's examiners' reports: Easy where the report says most students scored well (60% or more of the marks), Hard where few did (under 35%). Parts the report gives no figure for are left unrated.</li>
    <li><strong>Key-term cards, the formula sheet summary and the notes on the required practicals and maths skills</strong> are the site's own writing, checked by our tutor; they are not copied from AQA's material.</li>
    <li><strong>Grade boundaries and exam dates</strong> are AQA's published figures.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>The tutoring is by Rosey, an A-level Physics teacher who teaches the AQA specification; see the <a href="/tutors/">tutor page</a>. The site is built and maintained by the same small team that runs <a href="https://www.alevelbiologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelbiologytutor.com</a>, <a href="https://www.mathsaleveltutor.com" rel="noopener">mathsaleveltutor.com</a> and <a href="https://www.alevelpsychologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelpsychologytutor.com</a>.</p>
  <h2>Mistakes</h2>
  <p>If you find one, tell us on the <a href="/report/">report a mistake</a> page; corrections usually go live the same week.</p>
</Base>
